  "Question": "If \\(a\\cdot b>0\\) and neither \\(a\\) nor \\(b\\) is a zero vector, what is the angle between them?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "A right angle",
    "B": "An obtuse angle",
    "C": "An acute angle",
    "D": "It must be 0 degrees"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The dot product equals \\(|a||b|\\cos\\theta\\). The magnitudes are positive, so a positive dot product implies \\(\\cos\\theta>0\\), and the angle is acute.",
